      "script": [
        "START GAME",
        "I set my pack down and tell the ferryman I'm called Wren, a mapmaker bound for the survey-house at Harrowgate, and that my map is due before the autumn fair.",
        "I take out my brass compass - the one with the cracked lid my mother left me - and take a bearing on the far bank.",
        "I ask the ferryman why the water makes no sound.",
        "I pick up a flat stone and skim it out across the gloamwater.",
        "I ask the eel-smoker what she's curing and whether she'll sell me one.",
        "I tie a tollow-knot in the loose end of the mooring rope for luck.",
        "I warm my hands at the firepit and mention that the ferry's lean worries me, since I cannot swim.",
        "I step toward the ferry.",
        "I ask the ferryman what he'd charge to take me across.",
        "I count out what he asked and hand it over.",
        "I read the notices nailed to the leaning post.",
        "I ask the ferryman about the strangest notice ever nailed to that post.",
        "I sit on the dock's edge and sketch the ferry into my map, exactly as it sits.",
        "I ask the eel-smoker if the crossing is safe with the raft leaning like that.",
        "I wait and watch the mist on the water.",
        "I keep waiting as the light starts to fail.",
        "I ask the ferryman whether he'll still cross this late.",
        "I ask the eel-smoker to share her fire for the night, and offer to turn the eels while she rests.",
        "I eat some hard bread from my pack and listen to the river say nothing.",
        "I check my pack over by firelight to be sure nothing has gone missing.",
        "As the fire settles, I tell the eel-smoker where I'm bound and why the map cannot be late.",
        "I think back over the notices on the post and copy the strangest one into my map's margin.",
        "I ask her whether she has ever crossed at night, whatever the ferryman says.",
        "I bank the fire, tie one last tollow-knot in my bootlace, and settle in facing the water."
      ]
    },
